413667626678944, -0.00051456707296893, 0.014515180140733719, 0.005121283698827028, -0.02355465292930603, 0.02355465292930603, 0.023164458572864532, 0.005664302036166191, -0.03623592481017113, -0.00965077430009842, 0.0033182664774358273, 0.03813486546278, -0.01066527608782053, -0.050829146057367325, -0.011575726792216301, -0.017025422304868698, 0.01197892613708973, -0.027287498116493225, -0.011588732711970806, 0.008818362839519978, -0.001061650225892663, -0.0037556078750640154, 0.017662737518548965]], "input": ["# Rheological Properties and Viscosity in Food\n\nThis community focuses on the rheological properties of food, particularly viscosity, and their impact on food texture and swallowing. The entities are interconnected through their influence on the formation and perception of food boluses, which is crucial for safe consumption, especially for individuals with swallowing difficulties.\n\n## Rheological properties influence food texture and swallowing\n\nRheological properties are essential characteristics of food that affect its texture and consistency, which in turn influences sensory perception during swallowing. Understanding these properties is crucial for ensuring that food is safe and palatable, especially for individuals with dysphagia. The relationship between rheological properties and food bolus formation is significant, as it directly impacts how food is perceived and consumed. [Data: Entities (771); Relationships (1410)]\n\n## Viscosity as a key rheological property\n\nViscosity is a critical rheological property that describes a fluid's resistance to flow, playing a vital role in the behavior of food boluses. It affects how food moves and interacts within the digestive system, making it particularly important for modifying the texture of liquids for patients with dysphagia. This modification is essential to ensure safe consumption without the risk of aspiration or choking. [Data: Entities (728); Relationships (5019)]\n\n## Interconnection between viscosity and food bolus perception\n\nThe relationship between viscosity and rheological properties highlights how these factors influence the formation and perception of food boluses during swallowing. A better understanding of this interconnection can lead to improved food formulations that cater to individuals with specific dietary needs, particularly those with swallowing difficulties. [Data: Relationships (1410, 5019)]\n\n## Importance of rheological properties in food safety\n\nRheological properties are not only important for texture and sensory perception but also play a crucial role in food safety. By understanding how these properties affect swallowing, food manufacturers can create products that minimize the risk of choking and aspiration, particularly for vulnerable populations such as the elderly or those with medical conditions affecting swallowing. [Data: Entities (771, 728); Relationships (1410)]", "# Nutrition and Clinical Practice Community\n\nThe community is centered around a comprehensive bibliography that supports various guidelines and recommendations in nutrition and clinical practice. Key entities include the ESPGHAN Committee on Nutrition, notable researchers like Willett WC and Gibson RS, and various studies related to nutritional management in specific health conditions. These entities are interconnected through their contributions to nutritional guidelines and research, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in clinical settings.\n\n## BIBLIOGRAFÍA as a foundational resource\n\nBIBLIOGRAFÍA serves as a comprehensive collection of references that underpins various guidelines in nutrition and clinical practice. It includes studies on nutritional assessment methodologies and specific conditions such as Adrenoleukodystrophy and inflammatory bowel disease. This resource is vital for healthcare professionals, providing evidence-based information that supports clinical decisions regarding nutritional management. The bibliography's extensive references highlight its significance in the community, as it connects various entities and their contributions to the field. [Data: Entities (1420), Relationships (6300, 4346, 6297, 6298, 6299, +more)]\n\n## Role of ESPGHAN Committee on Nutrition\n\nThe ESPGHAN Committee on Nutrition is pivotal in developing guidelines focused on pediatric nutrition. Their recommendations are essential for healthcare professionals working with infants and children, ensuring that nutritional needs are met effectively. The committee's work is referenced in the BIBLIOGRAFÍA, indicating its influence on clinical practices and the importance of its guidelines in the community. This connection underscores the committee's role in shaping nutritional standards and practices for young patients. [Data: Entities (2497), Relationships (6297)]\n\n## Contributions of Willett WC to nutritional epidemiology\n\nWillett WC is a prominent figure in nutritional epidemiology, known for his research on dietary assessment methods and their impact on health outcomes. His work is frequently cited in the BIBLIOGRAFÍA, establishing him as a foundational reference in the field. The significance of his contributions lies in advancing the understanding of how dietary factors influence health, which is crucial for developing effective nutritional guidelines. This highlights the interconnectedness of research and clinical practice within the community. [Data: Entities (7658), Relationships (6298)]\n\n## Gibson RS's expertise in dietary assessment\n\nGibson RS is recognized for his expertise in nutritional assessment, particularly in measuring food consumption. His research is included in the BIBLIOGRAFÍA, emphasizing the importance of accurate dietary assessment in clinical practice. This expertise is vital for healthcare professionals to evaluate and address the nutritional needs of patients effectively. The inclusion of his work in the bibliography illustrates the collaborative nature of research and its applicat